    {"problem": "The bonus room over the garage is never the right temperature", "solution": "It has three cold surfaces: the floor over an unheated garage, the outside walls and the roof. We check its duct run and return air first, and when the ducts can't carry enough, a single ductless head gives that room its own heating and cooling."},
    {"problem": "The furnace starts up loud enough to interrupt a movie", "solution": "A single-stage furnace has one setting, and it's loud. A two-stage, variable-speed model starts on low fire and ramps up only when the house needs it, so most of the time you hear airflow, not a jet engine."},
    {"problem": "Static shocks and gaps in the hardwood every February", "solution": "Cold outdoor air holds little moisture, so indoor air dries out fast. A whole-home humidifier on the furnace keeps humidity steady, and we set it to drop on very cold days so windows don't fog."},
