  ("What does variable-speed mean on a furnace?", "A variable-speed furnace has a blower motor that adjusts its speed to the heat the house needs, instead of running full blast every cycle. In a large Ancaster home that means quieter operation, more even temperatures and better humidity control in summer."),
  ("Is zoning worth it in a large Ancaster home?", "It's worth it when parts of the house stay a few degrees apart even after the ducts are balanced. Zoning works best with two-stage or variable-speed equipment, so the system can run gently when only one zone calls."),
  ("What indoor humidity should I aim for in winter?", "Most Ontario homes are comfortable around 30% to 40% relative humidity in winter, set lower during very cold spells to avoid condensation on windows. Pair the humidifier with an outdoor temperature sensor and it makes that adjustment on its own."),
  ("Can a cold-climate heat pump heat a big house on the escarpment?", "It can, as long as nobody guesses at the size: we work it out room by room with a heat-loss calculation. Models like the Midea EVOX G3 are rated to -30°C, and many larger homes pair one with a gas furnace for the coldest weeks."),
